      "title": "Halloween & Día de los Muertos Celebration",
      "description": "Celebrate Halloween & Dîa De Los Muertos with Us! \n\nBring your little ones in their costumes for a day of downtown Halloween fun!\nYou’ll enjoy family-friendly entertainment, music, crafts, trick-or-treating, and more during our Halloween & Dîa de los Muertos celebration!\nLook forward to these Halloween festivities:\n\nDía de los Muertos traditions\nLive Entertainment\nLocal businesses handing out treats*\nAnd a spectacular 12-minute drone show finale!\n\n\nHere’s the schedule:\n\nAfternoon: Downtown Trick-or-Treat (participating businesses will distribute treats)\n\n\nThe Día de los Muertos Cultural Experience:\n\nCommunity Altar Display\nPhoto Opportunities\nArts and Crafts Stations\nFace Painting inspired by Día de los Muertos traditions\nCandy Station\nDay of the Dead Bread and Hot Chocolate Station\nLive Entertainment\nEducational exhibits highlighting the meaning and history of the celebration will be present at the event or in the downtown area.\n\n\nThe Drone Show Grand Finale:\n\nOur Downtown Drone Show will showcase colorful Halloween & Día de los Muertos images!\n\n\nDon’t miss it!\n\n*Halloween treats available while supplies last.\nAurora Downtown District – where culture, creativity, and cuisine collide! From globally inspired cuisine and one-of-a-kind shops to live entertainment and inspiring public art, downtown Aurora is designed to be experienced. Just 45 minutes from Chicago, our downtown business district offers an urban vibe that’s bold, creative, and unmistakably Aurora. Welcome to Illinois’ second-largest city with a small-town feel!",
